GPL-2.0 is not a stylistic choice: modules/rootfs_data_part.c is a Linux kernel
module and links against GPL-2.0 kernel headers, so it could not be anything
else. The rest is kept under the same license for consistency.

Third-party components are not covered by the above, are not redistributed in
this kit, and are fetched from their own sources at build time:

  OpenWrt 21.02.7        github.com/openwrt/openwrt @ 57a6d97ddf8f...
                         GPL-2.0 and others, per package
  LuCI                   github.com/openwrt/luci @ e4c46338b196...
                         Apache-2.0
  OpenWrt packages feed  git.openwrt.org/feed/packages @ 48242ee7a190...
                         per package
  Linux 4.4.176          the Mercusys "GPL Code" drop for the MR60X v2
                         GPL-2.0
  hostapd / wpad         part of OpenWrt; patches/900-*.patch applies to it
                         BSD-3-Clause
  gpio-button-hotplug    the same GPL drop (originally OpenWrt, by Felix
                         Fietkau and Gabor Juhos), GPL-2.0

patches/900-rtl8192cd-sta-assoc-reply.patch modifies hostapd and is therefore
offered under hostapd's own BSD-3-Clause terms, not GPL-2.0.

RF calibration tables (etc/conf/rtl8832bre/RFE50/**, 39 files) are proprietary
vendor data. They are NOT in this kit and are not redistributed by it:
build_image.sh extracts them from the official Mercusys firmware image that you
download yourself. build_image.sh explains which files and why, at the step
that extracts them.

This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Mercusys or
TP-Link. Product names are used only to identify the hardware this software
runs on.
